n","locator":"footprints[1] ref R1 dnp=true; tracks list shows /IN copper ends at R1 pad 1 (104.0875,100) with no other /IN-to-/OUT conductor"},{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/fitted_connectivity.json","locator":"fitted_path_IN_to_OUT = false; islands list; r1_pad_gap_mm = 0.8"},{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 'Independent fitted-assembly DC connectivity check'"},{"path":"inputs/requirements.txt","locator":"line 1: fitted resistive DC path must connect /IN to /OUT; do not assume an unpopulated footprint conducts"}],"reasoning":"The requirement is explicit and the native files are unambiguous: both the schematic symbol and the board footprint for R1 carry the DNP attribute, and no alternate assembly override exists. My pcbnew-based analysis modeled only fitted conductors (fitted resistors bridge their pads; fitted capacitors are DC-open; DNP footprints conduct nothing) and corrected for a mid-segment track T-junction at (107.5,100) so the /OUT copper is fully merged; even so, /IN remains isolated. Zero-violation ERC/DRC exits do not contradict this because KiCad connectivity treats DNP pads as net members; a successful tool exit is not proof of electrical behavior. This directly fails the sole evaluated criterion, hence blocking."},{"id":"PHY-2","title":"Verification coverage gap: all packet checks pass while the sole functional criterion fails, because no check is assembly-population-aware","location":"packet checks erc/drc/netlist/geometry (work/erc/erc.json, work/drc/drc.json, work/netlist/connectivity.json, work/geometry/geometry.json)","condition":"The packet's four checks all report pass/info with zero violations on a board whose fitted assembly fails the stated /IN-to-/OUT requirement. ERC has no rule that a DNP part breaks a required path; DRC connectivity and schematic parity treat the DNP footprint's pads as valid net members (and dnp is set consistently in both files, so parity sees no mismatch); netlist and